      "writtenOn": "2021-12-22T23:00:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm, currently Scone use a custom context to add renounce permissions like this: https://source.corp.google.com/piper///depot/google3/java/com/google/android/apps/scone/utils/ContextPermissionsUtils.java;l\u003d29?q\u003drenounce\u0026sq\u003d\u0026ss\u003dpiper%2FGoogle%2FPiper:google3%2Fjava%2Fcom%2Fgoogle%2Fandroid%2Fapps%2Fscone%2F. It seems now that they are 2 ways to renounce permissions, one with passing booleans in parameters or/and adding renounce permissions in the context(This is more general and can applied to other cases that the current modified methods) but is only for privileged apps.",
      "parentUuid": "57c49b09_a4c7881a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11588,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 11593,
        "endChar": 74
      },
      "revId": "68f3835266401dd56366ebcda18dc4cd666dca86",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "75308bc8_50578346",
        "filename": "telephony/java/android/telephony/TelephonyManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 11593,
      "author": {
        "id": 1138358
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-22T23:10:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I can see that one doesn\u0027t need to use both this API \u0026 renouncedPermissions, i.e. it\u0027s a corner case. However we need to define APIs in a consistent way. If we claim getServiceState() honors RenouncedPermissions, wouldn\u0027t it be more natural for all its overrides to honor it?",
      "parentUuid": "9c471e5d_d513fa0f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11588,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 11593,
        "endChar": 74
      },
      "revId": "68f3835266401dd56366ebcda18dc4cd666dca86",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "955f33c4_0959bb13",
        "filename": "telephony/java/android/telephony/TelephonyManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 11593,
      "author": {
        "id": 1112039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-23T03:20:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But it gives a contradicting usecase when user explicitly passes false to renounce permission and then we look into context and then renounce it.",
      "parentUuid": "75308bc8_50578346",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11588,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 11593,
        "endChar": 74
      },
      "revId": "68f3835266401dd56366ebcda18dc4cd666dca86",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bf93d37e_b7aa6000",
        "filename": "telephony/java/android/telephony/TelephonyManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 11593,
      "author": {
        "id": 1138358
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-23T03:34:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "passing a false to this API just means do not _additionally_ renounce permission. It\u0027s just like if you don\u0027t already have the permission, passing a false doesn\u0027t grant you. I would say it\u0027s more contradicting if you can gain a permission from a context with renounced permission.",
      "parentUuid": "955f33c4_0959bb13",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11588,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 11593,
        "endChar": 74
      },
      "revId": "68f3835266401dd56366ebcda18dc4cd666dca86",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1f8484d9_ee4cbaa2",
        "filename": "telephony/java/android/telephony/TelephonyManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 11593,
      "author": {
        "id": 1112039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-23T05:09:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is contradicting either way. I think this will result in confusing behavior.",
      "parentUuid": "bf93d37e_b7aa6000",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11588,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 11593,
        "endChar": 74
      },
      "revId": "68f3835266401dd56366ebcda18dc4cd666dca86",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "191ad2c6_9e929397",
        "filename": "telephony/java/android/telephony/TelephonyManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 11593,
      "author": {
        "id": 1890690
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-23T17:45:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Personally I think because there will be 2 possible ways to renounce permissions for getting service state, it\u0027s better to \u0027merge\u0027 the 2. If they get a unexpected result, is kinda their \u0027fault\u0027 because they allow it and renounce, but if we remove one options to renounce for the api calls it will be the fault of the api(\u0027ours\u0027) because is not taking in consideration the possible ways to renounce. Ideally there\u0027s only one way to do it but it does not seems possible for the moment unless with remove renouncePermissions from the context.",
      "parentUuid": "1f8484d9_ee4cbaa2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11588,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 11593,
        "endChar": 74
      },
      "revId": "68f3835266401dd56366ebcda18dc4cd666dca86",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
